@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-training-duty`

-- g3-tests-training-duty.l4: tests of section 17, written by ENCODER G3.
--
-- Every expected value was decided from the Hebrew text of s.17 (inputs/law.wiki lines 144-150, checked against the gazette pages
-- 185 and 186: eight hours at least, three months) before the module was run.  Dates were counted with an independent calendar
-- script (python datetime).  The calendars of rest days are ILLUSTRATIONS.
--
-- The last year of validity counted back from the last day L is the days after the same day one year earlier, up to and including L:
-- for L = 31 March 2030 that is 1 April 2029 to 31 March 2030.  `-- TRACE-EXPECT:` lines are read by check-traces.py.

§ `Tests of section 17`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- Fields in order: day attended; hours; under the Ministry's supervision; conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division;
-- in the licensee's field; on a date the Registrar directed; attended as a course required under 17(b); requirements met.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      hours IS A NUMBER
      supervised IS A BOOLEAN
      recognised IS A BOOLEAN
      infield IS A BOOLEAN
      directed IS A BOOLEAN
      required IS A BOOLEAN
      met IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Training session attended`
`fixture — a session` day hours supervised recognised infield directed required met MEANS
    `Training session attended` WITH
        `the day attended` IS day
        `the licence was in force on the day attended` IS TRUE
        `hours attended` IS hours
        `held under the supervision of the Ministry` IS supervised
        `conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division` IS recognised
        `within the licensee's field of work under the licence` IS infield
        `held on a date the Registrar directed` IS directed
        `attended because the Registrar required that particular course under section 17(b)` IS required
        `the licensee met the requirements of the training` IS met

-- A session that qualifies in every respect and whose requirements were met.
GIVEN hours IS A NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Training session attended`
`fixture — a qualifying session` hours day MEANS
    `fixture — a session` day hours TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE

GIVETH A DATE
`fixture — the last day of validity` MEANS YMD 2030 3 31

GIVETH A DATE
`fixture — the last day of validity as extended by three months` MEANS YMD 2030 6 30

§§ `17(a). The day one year earlier, and the last year of validity`

-- "The same day one year earlier", clamped when the month lacks the day (the clamp is IL s.10(b)'s rule used by analogy, backwards: fork S17-B).
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the same day one year earlier than` (YMD 2030 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2029 3 31
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the same day one year earlier than` (YMD 2030 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2029 1 1
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the same day one year earlier than` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the same day one year earlier than` (YMD 2029 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 28
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the same day one year earlier than` (YMD 2028 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
-- The window for L = 31 March 2030 is 1 April 2029 to 31 March 2030, both ends inside.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2029 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31)
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2029 4 1) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31)
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2030 4 1) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31)
-- With an extension the window closes on the extended day: 1 April 2030 is in, 1 July 2030 is out (fork S17-A).
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2030 4 1) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30)
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2030 6 30) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2030 7 1) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30)
-- L = 29 February 2028: the window starts on 1 March 2027 (the same day a year before is clamped to 28 February 2027).
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2027 2 28) (YMD 2028 2 29) (YMD 2028 2 29)
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2028 2 29) (YMD 2028 2 29)
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2028 2 29) (YMD 2028 2 29) (YMD 2028 2 29)

§§ `17(a). The eight hours`

-- Eight hours is enough, and seven and a half are not: "at least" (kind Q).
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 10 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 7.5 (YMD 2029 10 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 7.99 (YMD 2029 10 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 9 (YMD 2029 10 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
-- Hours are summed over sessions: four and four are eight; four and three are not.
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 4 (YMD 2029 6 1), `fixture — a qualifying session` 4 (YMD 2030 1 15)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 4 (YMD 2029 6 1), `fixture — a qualifying session` 3 (YMD 2030 1 15)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the hours counted towards the eight hours` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 4 (YMD 2029 6 1), `fixture — a qualifying session` 3 (YMD 2030 1 15)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
-- Edges of the window: a session of eight hours on 1 April 2029 counts, one on 31 March 2029 does not; the closing day counts, the day after does not.
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 4 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 3 31)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2030 3 31)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2030 4 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
-- With an extension, what is attended up to the extended day counts (taken reading, fork S17-A): 1 April 2030 counts, 1 July 2030 does not.
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2030 4 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity as extended by three months`
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2030 6 30)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity as extended by three months`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2030 7 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity as extended by three months`
-- Alternative S17-A: the last year counted back from the extended day.  A session of 10 April 2029 is in the first window and not the second.
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 4 10)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity as extended by three months`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty was met, the last year counted back from the last day as extended` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 4 10)) `fixture — the last day of validity as extended by three months`
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty was met, the last year counted back from the last day as extended` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 7 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity as extended by three months`

§§ `17(a). What makes a session count`

-- Each condition of the text is needed: the Ministry's supervision; conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division;
-- the licensee's field under his licence; on a date the Registrar directed.  One session of eight hours, one condition missing at a time.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
-- A session that does not qualify does not count towards the hours but also does not trouble the requirements limb:
-- eight qualifying hours with requirements met, plus three hours that were not under the Ministry's supervision and whose requirements were not met.
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 10 1), `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 11 1) 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
-- "And shall meet the requirements of those trainings": eight qualifying hours whose requirements were not met.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
-- Alternative S17-D discriminates: eight qualifying hours met, plus two qualifying hours whose requirements were not met.
-- Taken reading: the requirements limb reaches every qualifying session, so the duty is not met.  Alternative: a session counts only if met, so it is.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 10 1), `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 11 1) 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty was met, a session counting only if its requirements were met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 10 1), `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 11 1) 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
-- Under the alternative eight hours not met are still not enough.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty was met, a session counting only if its requirements were met` (LIST `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
-- (b) says "in addition to the trainings under subsection (a)": a course required under (b) does not count towards the eight hours (fork S17-C).
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty was met, counting a course required under section 17(b) as well` (LIST `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
-- A required course counts with other sessions under the alternative only as far as it qualifies otherwise.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty was met, counting a course required under section 17(b) as well` (LIST `fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
-- Alternative S17-E: the sources give the licensee no excuse when no training was available; the alternative would excuse him.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity`
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty was met, or no qualifying training was available` EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty was met, or no qualifying training was available` EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` FALSE
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty was met, or no qualifying training was available` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 10 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` FALSE

-- Fork S17-W: a session on a day the licence was not in force is not "during its validity".  A temporary licence for six months from 1 April 2030
-- has a term ending 30 September 2030, and the twelve months back from that day begin on 1 October 2029, a long time before the licence did.
-- Training of 20 March 2030, inside those twelve months but before the licence began, does not count.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      hours IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Training session attended`
`fixture — a qualifying session before the licence began` day hours MEANS
    `Training session attended` WITH
        `the day attended` IS day
        `the licence was in force on the day attended` IS FALSE
        `hours attended` IS hours
        `held under the supervision of the Ministry` IS TRUE
        `conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division` IS TRUE
        `within the licensee's field of work under the licence` IS TRUE
        `held on a date the Registrar directed` IS TRUE
        `attended because the Registrar required that particular course under section 17(b)` IS FALSE
        `the licensee met the requirements of the training` IS TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session before the licence began` (YMD 2030 3 20) 8) (YMD 2030 9 30) (YMD 2030 9 30)
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2030 5 1)) (YMD 2030 9 30) (YMD 2030 9 30)
-- Hours before the licence began are not added to those after it: 4 hours before and 4 after are not eight.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session before the licence began` (YMD 2030 3 20) 4, `fixture — a qualifying session` 4 (YMD 2030 5 1)) (YMD 2030 9 30) (YMD 2030 9 30)
-- The reading that does not clip (the caller marks the licence in force on the day) counts them: 4 and 4 are eight.
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 4 (YMD 2030 3 20), `fixture — a qualifying session` 4 (YMD 2030 5 1)) (YMD 2030 9 30) (YMD 2030 9 30)

§§ `17(a). The duty as a rule`

-- Day 0 is the anniversary day, 31 March 2029, the day before the window opens; day 1 is 1 April 2029 and the last day, 31 March 2030, is day 365.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.17(a) — the licensee must attend eight hours of qualifying training in the last year of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `complete the eight hours of qualifying training in the last year of validity and meet its requirements` AT 365
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.17(a): the licensee did not attend eight hours of qualifying training
#TRACE `s.17(a) — the licensee must attend eight hours of qualifying training in the last year of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `complete the eight hours of qualifying training in the last year of validity and meet its requirements` AT 366
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.17(a): the licensee did not attend eight hours of qualifying training
#TRACE `s.17(a) — the licensee must attend eight hours of qualifying training in the last year of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 366)
-- With the extension the window closes on 30 June 2030: 456 days from 31 March 2029.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.17(a) — the licensee must attend eight hours of qualifying training in the last year of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity as extended by three months` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `complete the eight hours of qualifying training in the last year of validity and meet its requirements` AT 456
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.17(a): the licensee did not attend eight hours of qualifying training
#TRACE `s.17(a) — the licensee must attend eight hours of qualifying training in the last year of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity as extended by three months` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `complete the eight hours of qualifying training in the last year of validity and meet its requirements` AT 457

§§ `17(b). A particular course required by the Registrar`

-- Fields in order: day of the course; day notice was given; conducted/recognised; Council consulted; Council's advice valid;
-- opinion that circumstances justify; opinion that attendance is required; notice a reasonable time before; attended; met requirements.
GIVEN `the day of the course` IS A DATE
      `the day notice of the requirement was given` IS A DATE
      conducted IS A BOOLEAN
      consulted IS A BOOLEAN
      valid IS A BOOLEAN
      justified IS A BOOLEAN
      required IS A BOOLEAN
      reasonable IS A BOOLEAN
      attended IS A BOOLEAN
      met IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Particular course required under section 17(b)`
`fixture — a course` `the day of the course` `the day notice of the requirement was given` conducted consulted valid justified required reasonable attended met MEANS
    `Particular course required under section 17(b)` WITH
        `the day of the course` IS `the day of the course`
        `the day notice of the requirement was given` IS `the day notice of the requirement was given`
        `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division` IS conducted
        `the Council was consulted about requiring the course` IS consulted
        `the Council's advice about requiring the course was validly given` IS valid
        `in the Registrar's opinion circumstances justify requiring attendance` IS justified
        `in the Registrar's opinion attendance is required to train the licensee and to realise the purposes of the Law` IS required
        `notice was given a reasonable time before the date of the course` IS reasonable
        `the licensee attended the course` IS attended
        `the licensee met the requirements of the course` IS met

-- A course on 10 June 2027, notice on 1 May 2027 (40 days before), every condition met, attended and requirements met.
GIVETH A `Particular course required under section 17(b)`
`fixture — a sound course` MEANS `fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `s.17(b) — the Registrar has the power to require attendance at the course` `fixture — a sound course` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(b) — the licensee must attend the course` `fixture — a sound course` TRUE
-- Each condition of the text, one missing at a time: the course conducted by the Registrar or recognised; the Council consulted; its advice validly given;
-- the Registrar's finding of circumstances; his finding that attendance is required.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the Registrar has the power to require attendance at the course` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the Registrar has the power to require attendance at the course` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the Registrar has the power to require attendance at the course` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the Registrar has the power to require attendance at the course` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the Registrar has the power to require attendance at the course` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the Registrar has the power to require attendance at the course` `fixture — a sound course` FALSE
-- Notice that was not a reasonable time before the course: the power remains; the licensee's duty does not (taken, fork S17-F); the alternative keeps it.
#ASSERT `s.17(b) — the Registrar has the power to require attendance at the course` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 6 9) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the licensee must attend the course` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 6 9) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(b) — the licensee must attend the course, whether or not notice was given a reasonable time before` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 6 9) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE
-- Attendance and requirements are both needed.
#ASSERT `s.17(b) — the licensee attended the course and met its requirements` `fixture — a sound course`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the licensee attended the course and met its requirements` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the licensee attended the course and met its requirements` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Breach is on the day after the course: not yet on the day of the course.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the licensee breached the duty to attend the course as at` (YMD 2027 6 10) (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(b) — the licensee breached the duty to attend the course as at` (YMD 2027 6 11) (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(b) — the licensee breached the duty to attend the course as at` (YMD 2027 6 11) (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the licensee breached the duty to attend the course as at` (YMD 2027 6 11) `fixture — a sound course` TRUE
-- No duty, no breach: the Council was not consulted.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the licensee breached the duty to attend the course as at` (YMD 2027 6 11) (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE

-- The requirement is a power (MAY); the licensee's WITHIN is the days from the notice (1 May) to the course (10 June): 40.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.17(b) — the Registrar may require attendance at a particular course` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `require the licensee to attend a particular course` AT 0
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `attend the particular course and meet its requirements` AT 40
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.17(b): the licensee did not attend the particular course
#TRACE `s.17(b) — the Registrar may require attendance at a particular course` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `require the licensee to attend a particular course` AT 0
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `attend the particular course and meet its requirements` AT 41
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.17(b): the licensee did not attend the particular course
#TRACE `s.17(b) — the Registrar may require attendance at a particular course` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `require the licensee to attend a particular course` AT 0
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 41)
-- A requirement the Registrar had no power to make (the Council was not consulted): the rule owes nothing.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.17(b) — the Registrar may require attendance at a particular course` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Notice on the day of the course is the last day it could be a "reasonable time": the days counted are 0, and the licensee attends on day 0.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.17(b) — the licensee must attend the course the Registrar required` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 6 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `attend the particular course and meet its requirements` AT 0
-- Notice after the day of the course cannot be counted to: a named refusal.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s.17(b) — the licensee must attend the course the Registrar required` (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 6 11) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) BECAUSE "s.17(b): notice of the requirement was given after the day of the course, so no period can be counted to it"

§§ `17(c). Extension of the validity by up to three months`

-- Fields in order: day of the decision; the last day before any extension; the last day as it stands; the last day the extension fixes; duty unfulfilled;
-- Council consulted; its advice valid; Registrar's opinion special and justified; granted so that the licensee can fulfil the duty.
GIVEN `the day of the Registrar's decision` IS A DATE
      original IS A DATE
      current IS A DATE
      fixed IS A DATE
      unfulfilled IS A BOOLEAN
      consulted IS A BOOLEAN
      valid IS A BOOLEAN
      special IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Extension of validity under section 17(c)`
`fixture — an extension` `the day of the Registrar's decision` original current fixed unfulfilled consulted valid special purpose MEANS
    `Extension of validity under section 17(c)` WITH
        `the day of the Registrar's decision` IS `the day of the Registrar's decision`
        `the last day of validity before any extension under section 17(c)` IS original
        `the last day of validity as it stands when the decision is taken` IS current
        `the last day of validity fixed by the extension` IS fixed
        `the licensee had not fulfilled the duty under section 17(a) or (b)` IS unfulfilled
        `the Council was consulted about the extension` IS consulted
        `the Council's advice about the extension was validly given` IS valid
        `in the Registrar's opinion these are special cases and the circumstances are justified` IS special
        `the extension is granted so that the licensee can fulfil the duty` IS purpose

-- Decided on 15 March 2030, the last day 31 March 2030, extended to 30 June 2030, every condition met.
GIVETH A `Extension of validity under section 17(c)`
`fixture — a sound extension` MEANS `fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`fixture — 30 June 2030 is a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2030 6 30

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`fixture — 15 March 2030 is a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2030 3 15

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`fixture — 30 June and 1 July 2030 are days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2030 6 30, YMD 2030 7 1

-- The cap: three calendar months after the last day (IL s.10(b)), the month's last day if the month lacks the day.
-- 31 March 2030 + 3 months = 30 June 2030; 31 January 2030 + 3 months = 30 April 2030; 30 November 2030 + 3 months = 28 February 2031; 15 December 2030 + 3 months = 15 March 2031.
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the latest last day of validity after an extension of up to three months from` (YMD 2030 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2030 6 30
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the latest last day of validity after an extension of up to three months from` (YMD 2030 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2030 4 30
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the latest last day of validity after an extension of up to three months from` (YMD 2030 11 30) EQUALS YMD 2031 2 28
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the latest last day of validity after an extension of up to three months from` (YMD 2030 12 15) EQUALS YMD 2031 3 15
-- Kind V (a period of validity): IL s.10(c) is not applied, so a cap on a day of rest stays; the alternative moves it (fork S17-V).
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the latest last day of validity after an extension of up to three months from` (YMD 2030 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2030 6 30
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the latest last day of validity, with IL s.10(c) applied, after an extension of up to three months from` (YMD 2030 3 31) `fixture — 30 June 2030 is a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2030 7 1
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the latest last day of validity, with IL s.10(c) applied, after an extension of up to three months from` (YMD 2030 3 31) `fixture — 30 June and 1 July 2030 are days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2030 7 2
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the latest last day of validity, with IL s.10(c) applied, after an extension of up to three months from` (YMD 2030 3 31) `fixture — 15 March 2030 is a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2030 6 30

-- The extension is within the cap when it moves the end later and no later than the cap.
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the extension is for a period not exceeding three months` `fixture — a sound extension`
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the extension is for a period not exceeding three months` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 4 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the extension is for a period not exceeding three months` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 7 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- An extension that does not move the end, or moves it back, is no extension.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the extension is for a period not exceeding three months` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the extension is for a period not exceeding three months` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- A cap that begins on a month end: 31 January 2030 extended to 30 April 2030 is within, to 1 May 2030 is not.
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the extension is for a period not exceeding three months` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 1 15) (YMD 2030 1 31) (YMD 2030 1 31) (YMD 2030 4 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the extension is for a period not exceeding three months` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 1 15) (YMD 2030 1 31) (YMD 2030 1 31) (YMD 2030 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- The Registrar may extend only when every condition of the text holds.
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` `fixture — a sound extension` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` `fixture — a sound extension` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 7 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
-- Timing (taken, fork S17-T): decided on the last day it is in time, decided on the day after it is not; the alternative allows both.
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 4 1) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence, whenever the decision is taken` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 4 1) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
-- Fork S17-V2: a second extension.  After a first extension to 30 June 2030 the Registrar extends again to 30 September 2030 (three months from the
-- current end).  Taken, each extension is capped from the end as it stands; alternative, the three months are cumulative from the original end.
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 6 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) (YMD 2030 9 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence, the three months being cumulative` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 6 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) (YMD 2030 9 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence, the three months being cumulative` `fixture — a sound extension` TRUE
-- T25: section 8 limits validity to 31 March of the fifth year.  The extension to 30 June passes it.  Taken: allowed.  Alternative S17-M: capped at the limit.
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` `fixture — a sound extension` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence, no later than the limit of section 8` `fixture — a sound extension` TRUE (YMD 2030 3 31)
-- A limit later than the extension lets the alternative allow it; a limit equal to the extended day too.
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence, no later than the limit of section 8` `fixture — a sound extension` TRUE (YMD 2030 6 30)
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence, no later than the limit of section 8` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE (YMD 2030 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence, no later than the limit of section 8` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 4 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE (YMD 2030 3 31)

-- The power as a rule: with every condition the permission stands (MAY, no deadline); without, nothing is owed.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | extend the validity of the licence by up to three months
#TRACE `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence by up to three months` `fixture — a sound extension` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence by up to three months` `fixture — a sound extension` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `extend the validity of the licence by up to three months` AT 5
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence by up to three months` (`fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `17(d). The duty is a licence condition`

-- (a): breached only when the window has closed without the hours.  Window closes 31 March 2030.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(a) was breached as at` (YMD 2030 3 31) EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(a) was breached as at` (YMD 2030 4 1) EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(a) was breached as at` (YMD 2030 4 1) (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 10 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` TRUE
-- With the extension the window is open until 30 June 2030.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(a) was breached as at` (YMD 2030 6 30) EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity as extended by three months` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(a) was breached as at` (YMD 2030 7 1) EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity as extended by three months` TRUE
-- Before commencement for the work there is no condition.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(a) was breached as at` (YMD 2030 7 1) EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` FALSE
-- Alternative S17-d: read as binding from the first day of the last year, the condition is breached from 1 April 2029 until the eight hours are met.
-- The reading taken finds no breach before the window has closed.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(a) was breached as at` (YMD 2029 10 1) EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(d) — the condition of section 17(a), read as binding from the first day of the last year, was breached as at` (YMD 2029 10 1) EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the condition of section 17(a), read as binding from the first day of the last year, was breached as at` (YMD 2029 3 31) EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(d) — the condition of section 17(a), read as binding from the first day of the last year, was breached as at` (YMD 2029 4 1) EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the condition of section 17(a), read as binding from the first day of the last year, was breached as at` (YMD 2029 10 1) (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 9 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the condition of section 17(a), read as binding from the first day of the last year, was breached as at` (YMD 2029 10 1) EMPTY `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` FALSE

-- (b): breached after the day of the course by a licensee bound to attend who did not.
#ASSERT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(b) was breached as at` (YMD 2027 6 11) (LIST (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(b) was breached as at` (YMD 2027 6 10) (LIST (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(b) was breached as at` (YMD 2027 6 11) (LIST `fixture — a sound course`) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(b) was breached as at` (YMD 2027 6 11) EMPTY TRUE
-- The whole condition: either duty breached.
#ASSERT `s.17(d) — the licensee breached a licence condition through the training duty as at` (YMD 2030 4 1) EMPTY (`fixture — the last day of validity`) `fixture — the last day of validity` EMPTY TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(d) — the licensee breached a licence condition through the training duty as at` (YMD 2030 4 1) (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 10 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` (LIST (`fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(d) — the licensee breached a licence condition through the training duty as at` (YMD 2030 4 1) (LIST `fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 10 1)) `fixture — the last day of validity` `fixture — the last day of validity` (LIST `fixture — a sound course`) TRUE

§§ `17(e). The Registrar must ensure that trainings exist and are available`

-- The duty is performed when the trainings exist and are available; either alone is not enough.
#ASSERT `s.17(e) — the Registrar has ensured that the trainings exist and are available` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(e) — the Registrar has ensured that the trainings exist and are available` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(e) — the Registrar has ensured that the trainings exist and are available` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(e) — the Registrar has ensured that the trainings exist and are available` FALSE FALSE
-- No time is stated, so the duty stands until performed, and performing it, personally or through another, discharges it.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | ensure that the trainings exist and are available
#TRACE `s.17(e) — the Registrar must ensure that the trainings exist and are available` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.17(e) — the Registrar must ensure that the trainings exist and are available` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `ensure that the trainings exist and are available` AT 400

§§ `17(f). The Registrar must publish the trainings`

GIVEN `the day of the training` IS A DATE
      `the day it was published on the Ministry website` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the publication was a reasonable time before the training` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Training offered`
`fixture — a training` `the day of the training` `the day it was published on the Ministry website` `the publication was a reasonable time before the training` MEANS
    `Training offered` WITH
        `the day of the training` IS `the day of the training`
        `the day it was published on the Ministry website` IS `the day it was published on the Ministry website`
        `the publication was a reasonable time before the training` IS `the publication was a reasonable time before the training`

-- "A reasonable time before the date of the training" (kind N, not a period): published before the day of the training AND judged a reasonable time.
#ASSERT `s.17(f) — the Registrar published the training in good time` (`fixture — a training` (YMD 2027 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2027 5 1)) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(f) — the Registrar published the training in good time` (`fixture — a training` (YMD 2027 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2027 5 1)) FALSE)
-- Published the day before the training: before it, so the judgement decides; published on the day itself or after: not before.
#ASSERT `s.17(f) — the Registrar published the training in good time` (`fixture — a training` (YMD 2027 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2027 6 9)) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(f) — the Registrar published the training in good time` (`fixture — a training` (YMD 2027 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2027 6 10)) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(f) — the Registrar published the training in good time` (`fixture — a training` (YMD 2027 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2027 6 11)) TRUE)
-- Not published at all.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(f) — the Registrar published the training in good time` (`fixture — a training` (YMD 2027 6 10) NOTHING TRUE)
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | publish a training on the Ministry website
#TRACE `s.17(f) — the Registrar must publish the trainings on the Ministry website` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.17(f) — the Registrar must publish the trainings on the Ministry website` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `publish a training on the Ministry website` AT 3
